WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.096
The CIS Controls cover a wide range of security topics including asset management,

00:00:05.096 --> 00:00:08.171
access control, vulnerability management, logging, monitoring, incident response,

00:00:08.171 --> 00:00:10.093
security awareness, and data protection.

00:00:10.093 --> 00:00:13.936
Together, these areas help organizations establish a balanced security program.

00:00:13.936 --> 00:00:18.932
A program that only focuses on one area may leave important gaps elsewhere.

00:00:18.932 --> 00:00:23.544
For example, asset inventory helps teams know what they need to protect.

00:00:23.544 --> 00:00:26.234
Access control limits who can use systems.

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:28.540
Vulnerability management helps reduce known weaknesses.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:30.846
Logging and monitoring help detect problems.

00:00:30.846 --> 00:00:35.458
Control families make the broader program easier to understand because they connect

00:00:35.458 --> 00:00:37.380
individual safeguards to security outcomes.
